{
  "table_id": "Table_1",
  "display_number": "1",
  "title": "Table 1. Baseline characteristics of participants categorised by descriptive EVI and O₃ exposure-pattern groups.",
  "panel": "",
  "panel_title": "",
  "notes_before": [],
  "notes_after": [
    "Data are presented as mean (s.d.) or number (percentage), unless stated otherwise. Abbreviations: BA, biological age; BAA, biological age acceleration; BMI, body mass index; EVI, enhanced vegetation index; O₃, ozone. BMI summaries exclude three implausible baseline values outside the plausible range of 12–60 kg m⁻² (N = 3,194 for the BMI row). EVI and O₃ exposure-pattern groups were defined independently from their respective long-term exposure histories and are descriptive groupings rather than the primary continuous exposure estimands."
  ],
